From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] install the daemon where its own service file looks for it
Upstream-Status: Pending

meson installs virtual-media to bindir, while
xyz.openbmc_project.VirtualMedia.service in the same tree says
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/virtual-media. Nothing catches the contradiction at build
time; it surfaces only on the target as the unit failing with status=203/EXEC.

sbindir is the correct location for a system daemon with no user-facing CLI,
so move the install there rather than editing the unit. Fixing it here rather
than relocating the file from the packaging recipe keeps it fixed for every
consumer, and avoids a do_install mv that would silently leave any future
bindir binary unpackaged.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index a88482b..36767c5 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ srcfiles_app = [ 'src/main.cpp',
                  'src/state/activating_state.cpp',
                ]
 
-bindir = get_option('prefix') + '/' +get_option('bindir')
+sbindir = get_option('prefix') + '/' +get_option('sbindir')
 
 if get_option('legacy-mode').enabled()
   add_project_arguments(
@@ -217,7 +217,7 @@ executable('virtual-media',
            ],
            include_directories: incdir,
            install: true,
-           install_dir:bindir)
+           install_dir:sbindir)
 
 #Tests are placed in the tests folder, with it's own meson.build
 if (get_option('tests').enabled())
